{"r.log.Error is used for informational diagnostic messages that describe normal cleanup progress, not actual errors - this will flood the error log with false-alarm messages on every cleanup cycle and trigger monitoring alerts unnecessarily. Should use r.log.Debug or r.log.Info instead.": 0.9838718175888062, "The cleanup ticker interval was changed from 10 minutes to 1 minute, which appears to be a debugging artifact. With the 9-minute job timeout unchanged, if cleanup takes longer than 1 minute the next tick will be queued causing near-continuous cleanup runs and keeping the database under continuous delete pressure.": 0.9644609093666077, "Logging the entire ID slice with 'ids', ids can produce enormous log lines - with batch sizes of 32,767 IDs, a single log line could contain tens of thousands of integers, which will balloon log storage and slow down log shipping in production.": 0.9595741629600525}